# bug=K02 code=2 methods=MLWL,MLPB
# Vertebrate mitochondrial code (2): ATA and ATG are both Met, so the pair differs by synonymous changes only
# (ATA/ATG, GCT/GCC) and NG, LWL, LPB and YN give dN = 0. MLWL and MLPB count ATA <-> ATG as nonsynonymous
# (Tzeng et al.'s rule for the standard code, where ATA is Ile): dN 0.1538 and 0.1373.
k2
ATAGCTAAACTGGGT
ATGGCCAAACTGGGT

